{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QAnalysisUniquenessCounterexamples","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QAnalysisUniquenessCounterexamples","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QAnalysis"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.QDilogarithm.nonempty_of_addZeroClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.QDilogarithm.nonempty_of_addZeroClass","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QAnalysisUniquenessCounterexamples.lean#L150-L167","doc":"The repaired statement, with **no axiom**: over an `AddZeroClass` the\ntype is inhabited.\n\nThis is what the Lean existence claim always said, and it is worth\nbeing plain that it is much weaker than the proposition's prose: the\nwitness is the all-zero record, so this establishes *inhabitation of\nthe structure*, not the shuffle-recursion construction of the\nq-dilogarithm.  The same caveat applies to the two\n`exists_in_shuffle_hopf` theorems, which say so themselves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.not_qDilogarithm_exists_over_every_add_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.not_qDilogarithm_exists_over_every_add_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QAnalysisUniquenessCounterexamples.lean#L143-L148","doc":"**`QDilogarithm.exists_axiom` is false** as stated: a\n`QDilogarithm Empty` would have to supply `log_q : Empty`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.instAddEmpty_folio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.instAddEmpty_folio","kind":"instance","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QAnalysisUniquenessCounterexamples.lean#L139-L141","doc":"`Empty` carries an `Add`; the axiom quantified over every such\ncarrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.not_qLogarithm_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.not_qLogarithm_unique","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QAnalysisUniquenessCounterexamples.lean#L128-L135","doc":"**`QLogarithm.unique_axiom` is false**: `qlog 0` and `qlog 1` agree\non `coprod`, `counit` and `one` and differ in `log_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.not_qExponential_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.not_qExponential_unique","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QAnalysisUniquenessCounterexamples.lean#L118-L126","doc":"**`QExponential.unique_axiom` is false** -- in both files that\ndeclared it: `qexp 0` and `qexp 1` agree on `coprod`, `counit` and\n`D_q` and differ in `e_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.not_qDilogarithm_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.not_qDilogarithm_unique","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QAnalysisUniquenessCounterexamples.lean#L108-L116","doc":"**`QDilogarithm.unique_axiom` is false**, and so is its verbatim twin\n`QDilogarithm.unique_up_to_shift_axiom`: `dilog 0` and `dilog 1`\nagree on `log_q`, `mul`, `compl` and `div` and differ in `Li2.1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.qlog","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.qlog","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QAnalysisUniquenessCounterexamples.lean#L96-L104","doc":"A `QLogarithm ℕ` with primitive `c`, by the same construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.qexp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.qexp","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QAnalysisUniquenessCounterexamples.lean#L84-L94","doc":"A `QExponential ℕ` with grouplike `c`.  `coprod := fun x => (x, x)`\nmakes `grouplike` hold for every `c`; the constant counit and\n`D_q := id` do the same for the other two fields. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.dilog","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QAnalysisCounterexamples.dilog","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/QAnalysisUniquenessCounterexamples.lean#L72-L82","doc":"A pentagon-satisfying `QDilogarithm ℕ` whose `Li2` first component is\n`c`.  Every field other than `Li2` is independent of `c`, and\n`pentagon` holds because `Li2_eval` is constantly `0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}